00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:42.000
It was known as the Silver Book Plan, and it was, essentially, to raise Skid Row. Kick everyone out, bulldoze buildings, start fresh. Of course, residents of Skid Row and their advocates didn't like this new plan, and they began thinking about how to fight it. One of those people was Charles L. Sesser, a young lawyer at the time, who remembers coming across some research that showed that when you bulldoze a neighborhood like Skid Row, it just means more Skid Row-like neighborhoods pop up elsewhere. Well, we weren't quite sure whether it was true or not.
它被称为“银书计划”（Silver Book Plan），本质上是要夷平斯基德罗。把每个人赶走，推倒建筑物，重新开始。当然，斯基德罗的居民和他们的倡导者不喜欢这个新计划，他们开始考虑如何反击。其中一个人是查尔斯·L·塞瑟（Charles L. Sesser），当时的一位年轻律师，他记得偶然发现了一些研究，表明当你推倒像斯基德罗这样的社区时，这只是意味着更多类似斯基德罗的社区会在其他地方涌现。嗯，我们不太确定这是不是真的。

16
