Here's L. Sesser admitting that, true or not, the theory was useful. But it was a very useful theory for purposes of saying this is a mistake, that that whole idea was a mistake. The theory that Skid Row would just pop up somewhere else if residents were forced to move scared people who didn't want Skid Row's residents to end up in their neighborhood. Some of these scared people joined the Skid Row activists' cause, and the activists were happy to have them. We really did, you know, come up with this idea that had some scholarly support, but
这是塞瑟承认，无论真假，这个理论很有用。但对于说这是一个错误，整个想法是一个错误来说，这是一个非常有用的理论。如果居民被迫搬迁，斯基德罗就会在其他地方涌现的理论，吓坏了那些不希望斯基德罗居民最终出现在他们社区的人。一些被吓坏的人加入了斯基德罗活动人士的事业，活动人士很高兴有他们加入。我们确实，你知道，提出了这个有一定学术支持的想法，但

