have been longtime advocates for the homeless. They run a well-known soup kitchen in Skid Row called the Hippie Kitchen. The Blue Book plan was this, to contain the spread of Skid Row. It's basically what's called the containment plan. This new plan, we'll call it the containment plan from here on out, proposed some pretty radical ideas, including getting all the missions and the charities and other homeless services to physically move their offices so they'd be within the newly drawn borders of Skid Row.
一直是无家可归者的长期倡导者。他们在斯基德罗经营着一家著名的救济厨房，叫“嬉皮厨房”（Hippie Kitchen）。“蓝书计划”就是这样，旨在遏制斯基德罗的蔓延。这基本上就是所谓的“遏制计划”。这个新计划——我们从现在起称之为“遏制计划”——提出了一些相当激进的想法，包括让所有的使团、慈善机构和其他无家可归者服务机构在物理上搬迁他们的办公室，这样他们就会在斯基德罗新划定的边界内。

19
00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:39.000
Again, Gary Blasey. The deal was all the services that tend to attract homeless people will be concentrated to the east of Spring Street. And in exchange for that, the redevelopment agency will not only not bulldoze all of the SROs, but it will also fund a separate nonprofit called the SRO Housing. The SRO Housing Trust would be charged
